  "policy": "# Direct deployed lexical competition\n\nThe source-balanced binary baseline trades off target sensitivity and nearword false wakes; positive latent-command support increases both Jenny hits and false wakes, while negative peak risk reduces both. Neither is an overall improvement. Historical character/phone/phrase training-only auxiliary losses and paired phrase ranking also failed. These motivate testing a different deployed decision function, not a diagnosis that the binary head is uniquely responsible.\n\nReplace only the original3480\u21921 sigmoid head with3480\u21926 softmax: background, Nyx, Nick, Next, Mix, Muse. Deployment emits only Nyx probability, keeping all six logits in its denominator via weight-free reshape/crop/flatten. Parameter count25981\u219243386, original31variable encoder/head layout,15trainable tensors after frozenBN. This is a direct competing-class deployed head, not an auxiliary classifier discarded at export or a larger nonlinear binary head. Actual INT8 size/resource behavior must be measured, not inferred from parameter count.\n\nUse original initializer for the encoder, fresh Glorot head seed2726/zero biases, original source-balanced input sampler seed726/lexical727, Adam1e-5/20000fixed-final-only4090updates. No failed-final warm start, BNaffine/nonlinear/latent-positive/negative-peak combination. No TTS, human listening or development examples in training.\n\nAll original positive steps use classNyx and weight1; original startup negatives/background and other negative presentations use classbackground and weight20. For exactly eight original source-balanced bare lexical negative rows, retain their whole-time negative supervision/weight20, but label generated complete-container+3..27feature-hop reference region with that row's known Nick/Next/Mix/Muse class, background elsewhere. This changes categorical labels and deployment head together; do not claim isolated causality. Input schedule/source draws remain original. Source label comes only from immutable training metadata keyed by offset, never detector scores. Inventory confirms31644 existing bare lexical rows,15engine/class groups and valid endpoint regions; Qwen has fewer exact matched negatives, existing source-balanced fallback remains unchanged. Generated endpoints are process metadata, not human phonetic truth. Other40 synthetic negatives stay background even if they contain lexical material: this partial label coverage is explicit and may limit learning; no inferred relabeling.\n\nUse sparse categorical cross entropy with original region weights. No extra auxiliary term, class coefficient, temperature, margin or threshold selection. Competing classes may still learn source/carrier shortcuts or suppress Nyx; successful class training alone is not wakeword recognition evidence. No numerical equality audit, coefficient/threshold/checkpoint/seed/calibration rescue.\n\nBefore original training: implement actual label mapping and trainer, basic actual model construction/interface, and push exact execution lock. After training: one builtinINT8 scalar-output export with standard six real-zero states/basic interface/reset/function checks; complete372legacy/408Jenny/360Joe waveform replay at fixed.91796875/smoothing5/continuous81600prime, reusing original baseline traces. Preserve all outcomes. No independent threshold/final acceptance claim from consumed development. Frozenv30 retained; final independent qualification and matched official HiESP comparison remain required.\n"
